Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0008.
FULL cudagraphs with eager tensor-parallel all-reduces (VLLM_FULL_GRAPH_EAGER_ALLREDUCE=1, default off): the V2 GPU
runner's FULL capture (CudaGraphManager.capture, the target model and the speculator alike) goes through
BreakableCUDAGraphCapture(allreduce_only=True), and GroupCoordinator._all_reduce_out_place, while such a capture is
open, ends the segment, runs the all-reduce eagerly with PyNccl into a graph-pool output buffer, records it for replay
and resumes capture (eager_all_reduce_break). Only the plain PyNccl path breaks; custom / symmetric-memory / FlashInfer
all-reduces stay captured. Ops decorated with eager_break_during_capture (active in this build: attention, the sparse
indexer) stay in the graph, since a FULL replay runs eager segments without a forward context; the exception is the
new eager_in_full_graph marker, set on DeepSeek-V4.1 Engram's prefetch start / finish, which fork and join the
prefetch side stream across segments (a capture segment cannot end with unjoined side-stream work) and need no
forward context. V4.1's mHC coefficient overlap (sm_100 only) keeps its side stream across the attention all-reduce,
so it is off under the flag. maybe_execute_in_parallel /
execute_in_parallel keep their aux-stream overlap in these captures (they fork and join inside one segment;
all-reduces issued inside them stay captured). Only the target model's graphs split (the speculator's small
forwards would turn launch-bound). Why: 2x DGX Spark, TP=2 over RoCE: a decode-size all-reduce costs 50-160 us inside a
CUDA graph vs 26-42 us eager, ~96 of them per DSpark-3 decode step; PIECEWISE graphs (attention eager too) cost 19%
end to end, so only the all-reduces may leave the graph.

